Third-party attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Grind is an independent implementation written against ISO/IEC 13818-1
(MPEG-2 Systems), which defines the transport stream. No third-party code is
incorporated, and nothing here is a port of another implementation.

Test fixtures under src/test/resources are generated locally by FFmpeg from
synthetic sources - its testsrc pattern generator and sine tone generator - so
they contain no third-party media. The commands that produce them are recorded
in the test that consumes them, so any fixture can be regenerated from scratch.

FFmpeg's ffprobe, and TSDuck where installed, are used as independent references
to cross-check what Grind reports about a stream. Neither is distributed with
this project nor linked against it.
